1. Methodology reference (no code copied)
-----------------------------------------
Project: "Logs: LLMs can understand and write neural network weights" — the log
release behind the blog post *Sparks of Weight Space Programming*.
Repository: https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs
Licence: CC BY 4.0 (per that repository's LICENSE), plus separate terms for its
model weights and third-party benchmarks.
Commit consulted while writing this project: 4d09ba6d6a7e891dd8063974dfe81b3d78e3494f

Concepts taken from that work (ideas and data formats, not source code):
  * bounded direct tensor editing of a small pretrained model, with no gradient
    descent and no fine-tuning (exp8_math);
  * a *budgeted* forward-pass tool that separates cheap generation passes from
    teacher-forced reads, so a search cannot burn unbounded compute
    (exp8_math/README.md, runs/p50c/state.json);
  * the sparse delta concept: store only changed entries (flat index + new bit
    pattern) plus the sha256 of the base and edited tensor, and rebuild exactly
    (exp8_math/code/make_edit_diff.py, apply_edit.py);
  * refusing edits to the embedding / final norm / output layer, and refusing a
    uniform rescale of a whole tensor (exp8_math/code/profiles.py "frozen",
    "refuse_rescale");
  * the accept-or-rollback loop driven by a held-out evaluation.

What this project does NOT contain: no file from that repository, no copied
function, no copied prompt text, and none of its mathematical weight edits.
Its exp8 deltas modify Qwen3.5-0.8B layers 15/19 `mlp.down_proj` for *math*; this
project targets Hindi/Hinglish and ships no pretrained deltas at all — every edit
is produced by a run you perform and is stored under `checkpoints/deltas/`.

If you redistribute this project together with material derived from that
repository, keep its CC BY 4.0 attribution.

